{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Overfitting.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Overfitting.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"overfitting overfitting","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Overfitting.md","fileName":"Overfitting.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Overfitting","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-06 00:13\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Neural Network Training]] · [[Statistical Learning and Validation]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Neural Network Training","Statistical Learning and Validation","Training Dataset","Training Epoch","Test Dataset","algorithms.epub","dataanalysisforthelifescienceswithr.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Overfitting.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Overfitting.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"overfitting overfitting","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Overfitting.md","fileName":"Overfitting.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Overfitting","heading":"Overfitting","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Overfitting occurs when a model conforms so closely to its [[Training Dataset]] that it performs poorly on unfamiliar examples. It resembles learning a fixed set of answers by rote without learning the reusable relationship needed to solve new problems.\n\nAdditional [[Training Epoch|training epochs]] can continue reducing training error while making generalization worse. Comparing performance against a withheld [[Test Dataset]] reveals this gap and helps determine when more fitting has stopped being useful.\n\nThe source illustrates the problem with k-nearest neighbors: using one neighbor classifies every training observation perfectly because each point is its own nearest neighbor, yet it performs poorly on new data. Training fit alone therefore rewards excessive flexibility.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Neural Network Training","Statistical Learning and Validation","Training Dataset","Training Epoch","Test Dataset","algorithms.epub","dataanalysisforthelifescienceswithr.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Overfitting.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Overfitting.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"overfitting overfitting","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Overfitting.md","fileName":"Overfitting.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Overfitting","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[algorithms.epub]]\n\n[[dataanalysisforthelifescienceswithr.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Neural Network Training","Statistical Learning and Validation","Training Dataset","Training Epoch","Test Dataset","algorithms.epub","dataanalysisforthelifescienceswithr.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}